**Neumann's Expansion of an Arbitrary Function in a Series of Bessel Functions**

\(f(z){=}a_{0}J_{0}(z){+}2\sum\limits_{k=1}^{\infty}a_{ik}J_{k}(z)\qquad(|z|{<}c)\)

where \(c\) is the distance of the nearest singularity of \(f(z)\) from \(z{=}0\),

\(a_{k}{=}\frac{1}{2\pi i}{\int}_{|t|=e^{\prime}}f(t)O_{k}(t)dt\qquad(0{<}c^{ \prime}{<}c)\)

and \(O_{k}(t)\) is Neumann's polynomial. The latter is defined by the generating function

\(\frac{1}{t{-}z}{=}J_{0}(z)O_{0}(t){+}2\sum\limits_{k=1}^{\infty}J_{k}(z)O_{k}( t)\qquad(|z|{<}|t|)\)

\(O_{n}(t)\) is a polynomial of degree \(n+1\) in \(1/t\); \(O_{0}(t){=}1/t\),

\(9.1.85\)

\(O_{n}(t){=}\frac{1}{4}\sum\limits_{k=0}^{\infty}\frac{n(n{-}k{-}1)!}{k!}{\left(\frac{2}{t}\right)^{n-2k+1}}\quad(n{\equiv}1,2,\ldots)\)

